# macOS
.DS_Store

# test dependencies, not shipped and not part of the builder
tests/node_modules/

# local editor and tool settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Screenshots used to check a widget against a real 360Learning page. They are
# how most of this builder's design decisions got measured, and they are also
# megabytes each, so they stay local.
Screenshot *.png

# The prototypes the hero banner and the Live training widget were built in
# before being merged into index.html. Kept on disk because they are readable
# history, ignored because they are dead: the shipped widgets have moved a long
# way past them, and the real risk is somebody editing a lab file believing it
# is the live one.
hero-lab.html
classroom-lab.html
cover-lab.html

# The layout lab's generated page, and only that. Its generator and its shell
# are tracked, because they are source: `node lab/build-lab.js` rebuilds this
# from index.html at any time.
#
# The rule above does not apply to it. Those three prototypes are ignored
# because they can drift from the shipped widget and be mistaken for it; this
# one is sliced out of index.html every build, so it cannot drift and there is
# nothing in it to edit by mistake.
lab/live-training-lab.html

# The design canvas the five Live training layouts came from, 2026-08-06. A
# 230kb bundle of gzipped base64 that has to be unpacked to read. The layouts
# shipped, and what changed on the way across is written up in index.html
# where it can be maintained, so this is provenance rather than a source.
Live training widget.html
